# A blocking accept or connect that times out, and what a full listen backlog does, are the host's (docs/design/decisions.md): the errno numbers and the backlog differ.
# These answers are interrexx's on macOS, recorded on a Mac; the oracle has not been run there.
# A blocking accept waits no longer than the socket's SO_RCVTIMEO and a
# blocking connect no longer than its SO_SNDTIMEO (PR 4 review I2): -1 with
# EAGAIN, and -1 with EINPROGRESS while the connection goes on (a listener
# with backlog 0 holds one connection, so the second cannot complete).
ruled
s = SockSocket('AF_INET', 'SOCK_STREAM', 0)
a.family = 'AF_INET'; a.port = 0; a.addr = '127.0.0.1'
call SockBind s, 'a.'
call SockListen s, 0
call SockGetSockName s, 'a.'
say SockSetSockOpt(s, 'SOL_SOCKET', 'SO_RCVTIMEO', 500)
t = time('r')
say SockAccept(s) SockSock_Errno() (time('e') >= 0.45) (time('e') < 2)
c0 = SockSocket('AF_INET', 'SOCK_STREAM', 0); say SockConnect(c0, 'a.')
c = SockSocket('AF_INET', 'SOCK_STREAM', 0)
say SockSetSockOpt(c, 'SOL_SOCKET', 'SO_SNDTIMEO', 500)
t = time('r')
say SockConnect(c, 'a.') SockSock_Errno() (time('e') >= 0.45) (time('e') < 2)
say SockConnect(c, 'a.') SockSock_Errno()
::requires 'rxsock' LIBRARY
----
rc 0
